  "finding": "Canonical optimized DataChannel D1 is ret; endpoint D1 writes its own table and tailcalls base D1. The C++ standard does not require post-destruction vptr bytes; requiring a persistent base table was an invalid portable test assumption. Native original D1 writes remain independently mandatory. Fix checks source lifetime effects and actual deallocation without inspecting dead host object representation."
